<Base title="Dataset coverage and sources | CostOfCare">
<h1>The data is the product.</h1><p class="sub">Our own extraction pipeline reads hospital-published machine-readable files. Every searchable price retains its original source and dates.</p>
<section class="coverage"><div><strong>{summary.providers}</strong><span>source files parsed</span></div><div><strong>{summary.cities}</strong><span>cities resolved</span></div><div><strong>{summary.rows}</strong><span>hospital / code records</span></div></section>
<h2>What is included today</h2><p>Published cash prices and explicit dollar-denominated insurance rates for {summary.procedures} target CPT codes, including MRI, blood tests, scans, office visits and procedures. Search filters insurers when that hospital actually publishes matching rates. We do not fill gaps with invented estimates.</p>
<h2>What these numbers mean</h2><p>Cash prices are the source's discounted cash charges. Insurance rates are negotiated charges across the source's plans. They are not your deductible, copay or final bill. A published insurer rate does not establish that a provider is in your plan's network.</p><p style="margin-top:12px">Ranges can include different settings, billing classes, modifiers and plans for the same CPT code. Facility fees, physicians, radiology interpretation, anesthesia, drugs and follow-up care may be billed separately. A procedure code is not necessarily a complete treatment bundle. Ask for a written estimate for your exact care.</p>
<h2>Refresh: separate the dates</h2><p>Each record shows the date the hospital says its file was updated and the date our pipeline extracted it. Rechecking a file today does not make its underlying prices new. The refresh workflow runs daily, attempts primary-source files, preserves successful snapshots when a source fails and records failures. The first full automated run is still being tested. A daily schedule is not a guarantee every source refreshes within 24 hours.</p>
<h2>Coverage is growing, not complete</h2><p>The source-discovery registry currently contains {summary.registry_locations} location records. Only successfully parsed source files appear in search. Some files cover multiple locations; we do not count those locations as independently verified price coverage. Missing data, blocked downloads and unsupported formats are not evidence that care is unavailable.</p><p style="margin-top:12px">We have not yet reached the nationwide thousands-of-hospitals target. Insurer Transparency in Coverage feeds, pharmacy prices, insurance eligibility and personal out-of-pocket estimates are not included in this release.</p>
<h2>Sources and downloads</h2><ul style="padding-left:20px"><li>Hospital-published MRFs, linked directly on every search result.</li><li><a href="https://referencesource.org/hospital-price-transparency-mrf-index/">ReferenceSource MRF URL index</a>, used as a discovery seed, not as a source of prices. Its license position is listed as unknown; we collect pricing from hospital sources rather than republishing its prose.</li><li><a href="https://www.cms.gov/priorities/key-initiatives/hospital-price-transparency">CMS Hospital Price Transparency</a>, the underlying reporting program.</li><li><a href="/data/dataset.json">Download current JSON dataset and failure audit</a>.</li></ul>
<p class="muted" style="margin-top:24px">Search dataset assembled: {summary.generated_at}. This is an early research tool, not medical, legal or financial advice.</p>
</Base>
